    <item>
      <title>The Downfall of the Golden City</title>
      <description>Today&apos;s legend is about the one sin that destroyed an empire. In the city of Hastinapura, the mighty kingdom of the Kurus, greed had become a disease that consumed all who dwelled within its walls. King Dhritarashtra, blinded by his own wealth and power, refused to share the throne with his rightful heir, Duryodhana. As the kingdom&apos;s wealth grew, so did the corruption and the greed. The people became obsessed with acquiring more and more, never satisfied with what they had. The once-great kingdom was now on the brink of collapse. But it was not just the people who were consumed by greed – even the gods themselves had become corrupt. The great sage, Drona, had become a pawn in the game of greed, using his divine knowledge to further his own interests. As the kingdom teetered on the edge of destruction, a great war loomed on the horizon. The Pandavas, led by the brave Arjuna, would soon challenge the Kauravas, and the fate of Hastinapura would be sealed. This is Greed – the insatiable hunger that destroys everything in its path. In a world where wealth and status are the ultimate goals, we must remember that true greatness lies not in what we have, but in who we are.</description>
